# What Vercel uploads for the marketing deploy.
#
# The project's root is the repository, because `apps/marketing` depends on `@dak/shared` through a
# `workspace:*` protocol and pnpm cannot resolve that from the subdirectory alone. That means the
# whole monorepo is in scope, and the whole monorepo is ~37,000 files - more than the 15,000-item
# upload limit - so the exclusions below are what makes the deploy possible at all.
#
# Each entry is something the marketing build provably does not read. Nothing here is excluded
# because it is large; it is excluded because building one Astro site cannot need it.

# Vendored upstream references, read-only and never imported. By far the largest thing here at
# ~22,000 files, and nothing in the build path resolves into it.
.repos

# Runtime state and build output. Regenerated in the build; uploading it only ships stale bytes.
node_modules
**/node_modules
apps/*/dist
apps/server/dist
apps/desktop/dist
dist
.vite-plus
**/.vite-plus

# Vercel's own build scratch, and the local auth link.
.vercel
.env.local

# DAK's own database, logs and user data. Never part of a static site.
.dak
*.sqlite

# The vendored CanvasKit snapshot. It is byte-pinned and re-fetched by scripts/canvas-vendor.ts,
# and it is a large binary that has no business in a website deploy.
packages/canvas-engine/upstream/src/canvaskit.wasm